(>> 1.2 Parallelogram Law, Triangle Law and Polygon Law of Forces) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Parallelogram Law of Forces: If two concurrent forces acting simultaneously at a) Tj
T*
(common point are represented in magnitude and direction by two adjacent sides of a) Tj
T*
(parallelogram, their resultant is represented by the diagonal passing through their) Tj
T*
(point of intersection.) Tj
T*
(Formula: R = sqrt\( P^2 + Q^2 + 2*P*Q*cos\(theta\) \), where theta is the angle between P) Tj
T*
(and Q.) Tj
T*
(Direction of Resultant \(alpha with respect to P\): tan\(alpha\) = \(Q * sin\(theta\)\) / \(P + Q) Tj
T*
(* cos\(theta\)\).) Tj
T*
(* Triangle Law of Forces: If two forces acting at a point are represented in) Tj
T*
(magnitude and direction by the two sides of a triangle taken in order, their) Tj
T*
(resultant is represented by the closing third side taken in the opposite order.) Tj
T*
(* Polygon Law of Forces: If a system of concurrent coplanar forces is represented in) Tj
T*
(magnitude and direction by the sides of a polygon taken in order, the closing side) Tj
T*
(taken in reverse order represents their resultant vector.) Tj
T*
() Tj
