(* Moment of a Force \(M\): The rotational tendency of a force about an axis or point:) Tj
T*
(M_O = F * d, where d is the perpendicular moment arm from O to the force line of) Tj
T*
(action. In vector notation: M_O = r x F.) Tj
T*
(* Varignon's Theorem \(Principle of Moments\): The moment of a force about any point) Tj
T*
(equals the algebraic sum of the moments of its constituent rectangular components) Tj
T*
(about the same point: M_O\(F\) = M_O\(Fx\) + M_O\(Fy\).) Tj
T*
(* Force Couple: A system consisting of two equal, opposite, and non-collinear) Tj
T*
(parallel forces separated by perpendicular distance d. The moment of a couple is a) Tj
T*
(free vector: M = F * d. Its magnitude is invariant with respect to the reference) Tj
T*
(origin.) Tj
T*
