T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: Four concurrent forces act at origin O: F1 = 50 kN at 30 deg in) Tj
T*
(Quadrant I; F2 = 80 kN at 45 deg in Quadrant II; F3 = 60 kN at 60 deg in Quadrant III;) Tj
T*
(F4 = 40 kN directed vertically downward along negative y-axis. Determine the resultant) Tj
T*
(magnitude and direction.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Resolve all forces into orthogonal components:) Tj
T*
(F1: F1x = + 50*cos\(30\) = + 43.30 kN, F1y = + 50*sin\(30\) = + 25.00 kN.) Tj
T*
(F2: F2x = - 80*cos\(45\) = - 56.57 kN, F2y = + 80*sin\(45\) = + 56.57 kN.) Tj
T*
(F3: F3x = - 60*cos\(60\) = - 30.00 kN, F3y = - 60*sin\(60\) = - 51.96 kN.) Tj
T*
(F4: F4x = 0.00 kN, F4y = - 40.00 kN.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Sum horizontal and vertical components:) Tj
T*
(Sigma Fx = 43.30 - 56.57 - 30.00 + 0 = - 43.27 kN.) Tj
T*
(Sigma Fy = 25.00 + 56.57 - 51.96 - 40.00 = - 10.39 kN.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Compute Resultant Magnitude and Direction:) Tj
T*
(R = sqrt\( \(-43.27\)^2 + \(-10.39\)^2 \) = sqrt\( 1872.29 + 107.95 \) = sqrt\(1980.24\) = 44.50) Tj
T*
(kN.) Tj
T*
(Direction: Both components are negative => Resultant lies in Quadrant III.) Tj
T*
(theta = atan\( |-10.39| / |-43.27| \) = atan\(0.2401\) = 13.50 deg below negative x-axis \(or) Tj
T*
(193.50 deg from positive x-axis\).) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Resultant force is 44.50 kN acting at 193.50 deg counterclockwise from the) Tj
T*
(positive x-axis.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([EXAMPLE 2: Equilibrium of Suspended Sphere using Lami's Theorem]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: A smooth uniform steel sphere of mass 100 kg \(weight W = 981 N\) and) Tj
T*
(radius r = 200 mm is suspended by a string of length L = 300 mm tied to a smooth) Tj
T*
(vertical wall. Determine: \(1\) Tension T in the string, \(2\) Normal reaction R_w exerted) Tj
T*
(by the wall on the sphere.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Establish geometry and angles:) Tj
T*
(Let O be center of sphere and A be tie point on wall. In right triangle O-Wall-A:) Tj
T*
(Hypotenuse OA = string length + sphere radius = 300 + 200 = 500 mm.) Tj
T*
(Horizontal adjacent side \(from center to wall contact point\) = radius r = 200 mm.) Tj
T*
(cos\(theta\) = 200 / 500 = 0.40 => theta = 66.42 deg \(angle of string with horizontal\), or) Tj
T*
(angle with vertical phi = 90 - 66.42 = 23.58 deg.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Free Body Diagram of the sphere:) Tj
T*
