(Three concurrent forces act at sphere center O:) Tj
T*
(- Weight W = 981 N acting vertically downward \(270 deg\).) Tj
T*
(- Normal reaction R_w acting horizontally to the right \(0 deg\) from the smooth wall.) Tj
T*
(- Cable tension T pulling up and left at angle phi = 23.58 deg to the vertical.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Compute angles between forces for Lami's Theorem:) Tj
T*
(Angle between R_w and W = 90 deg.) Tj
T*
(Angle between T and W = 180 - 23.58 = 156.42 deg.) Tj
T*
(Angle between T and R_w = 90 + 23.58 = 113.58 deg.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Apply Lami's Theorem:) Tj
T*
(T / sin\(90\) = R_w / sin\(156.42\) = W / sin\(113.58\).) Tj
T*
(T = 981 * \(sin\(90\) / sin\(113.58\)\) = 981 / 0.9165 = 1070.38 N.) Tj
T*
(R_w = 981 * \(sin\(156.42\) / sin\(113.58\)\) = 981 * \(0.4000 / 0.9165\) = 428.15 N.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Cable tension T = 1070.38 N, Wall reaction R_w = 428.15 N.) Tj
T*
