T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: A horizontal steel bracket ABCD is subjected to three vertical forces:) Tj
T*
(20 kN downward at x = 0 m \(A\); 40 kN upward at x = 2 m \(B\); 30 kN downward at x = 5 m) Tj
T*
(\(D\); and a concentrated clockwise couple of 50 kN-m at point C \(x = 3.5 m\). Determine) Tj
T*
(the magnitude, nature, and position of the single resultant force measured from point A.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Calculate Resultant Force Magnitude:) Tj
T*
(Since all forces are purely vertical: R = Sigma Fy = - 20 + 40 - 30 = - 10 kN \(acting) Tj
T*
(downward\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Calculate Algebraic Sum of Moments about Point A:) Tj
T*
(Taking counterclockwise as positive \(+\), clockwise as negative \(-\):) Tj
T*
(M_A = [ - 20 * 0 ] + [ + 40 * 2.0 ] + [ - 30 * 5.0 ] + [ - 50 \(couple\) ]) Tj
T*
(M_A = 0 + 80 - 150 - 50 = - 120 kN-m \(clockwise moment of 120 kN-m\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Apply Varignon's Theorem to locate resultant line of action:) Tj
T*
(M_A\(R\) = R * x_bar) Tj
T*
(Since R is downward \(-10 kN\), a downward force placed at distance x_bar to the right of) Tj
T*
(A produces a clockwise moment about A:) Tj
T*
(- 10 * x_bar = - 120 kN-m => x_bar = 120 / 10 = 12.0 m.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: The resultant is a single downward force of 10 kN located at a distance of) Tj
T*
(12.0 m to the right of point A.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
