(Solution Step 1: Equivalent point load for the distributed UDL:) Tj
T*
(Total load of UDL = w * length = 15 kN/m * 4.0 m = 60 kN.) Tj
T*
(Centroid of UDL is at its midpoint: x_udl = 4.0 / 2 = 2.0 m from support A.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Apply Moment Equilibrium about support A \(Sigma M_A = 0\):) Tj
T*
(Clockwise moments from loads = Counterclockwise moment from roller reaction R_B:) Tj
T*
(\(60 kN * 2.0 m\) + \(50 kN * 6.0 m\) - \(R_B * 8.0 m\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(120 + 300 - 8.0 * R_B = 0 => 8.0 * R_B = 420 kN-m.) Tj
T*
(R_B = 420 / 8.0 = 52.50 kN \(upward\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Apply Vertical Equilibrium \(Sigma Fy = 0\):) Tj
T*
(R_A + R_B - 60 - 50 = 0 => R_A + 52.50 = 110 kN.) Tj
T*
(R_A = 110 - 52.50 = 57.50 kN \(upward\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Horizontal Equilibrium \(Sigma Fx = 0\):) Tj
T*
(Since all loads are vertical and roller at B offers no horizontal resistance: H_A = 0) Tj
T*
(kN.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Support reactions are R_A = 57.50 kN \(vertical upward\), R_B = 52.50 kN) Tj
T*
(\(vertical upward\), H_A = 0 kN.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
